Map Implementation Details
==========================

Overview
--------
This document describes the full implementation of the homepage "Export Regions" world map section.
It covers:
- Data source and map library strategy
- Rendering approach
- Country highlighting logic
- Desktop/mobile interactions
- Styling and theme tokens
- File-by-file responsibilities
- Production/deployment notes


1. What We Use (Library + Dataset)
----------------------------------
Primary map source:
- `@svg-maps/world` dataset (country-level world map geometry)

Current integration model:
- The dataset is vendored locally as:
  - `src/assets/world-map-data.js`
- This file exports world map metadata and path geometry:
  - `viewBox`
  - `locations[]` with `id`, `name`, `path`

Important note:
- We are using the official `@svg-maps/world` map data format, but due install/network restrictions in this environment, the dataset is stored locally instead of imported from npm at runtime.
- Runtime does NOT depend on any external API or CDN for map rendering.

Why this is lightweight and production-safe:
- Pure SVG paths rendered in React
- No Google Maps, Leaflet, WebGL, or tile engines
- No paid API calls
- No runtime network dependency for map asset


2. Map Rendering Architecture
-----------------------------
Main component:
- `src/components/home/export-regions/ExportMap.jsx`

How rendering works:
1. Import local world map dataset from `src/assets/world-map-data.js`.
2. Normalize each country id to uppercase ISO-2 (e.g., `in` -> `IN`).
3. Build an in-memory `countries` array of:
   - `code` (ISO-2)
   - `d` (SVG path)
4. Render a single `<svg>` with one `<path>` per country.
5. Apply fill/stroke dynamically based on whether country is served.

SVG setup:
- `viewBox` comes from dataset (`worldMapData.viewBox`)
- `preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"` keeps geographic aspect ratio stable
- Map scales responsively through `w-full h-auto`


3. Country Highlighting Logic
-----------------------------
Served data source:
- `src/constants/servedRegions.js`

Current static shape (temporary by scope):
- `{ [ISO2]: string[] }`
- Example:
  - `IN: ["Gujarat", "Maharashtra", "Delhi"]`
  - `US: ["California", "Texas"]`
  - `DE: ["Bavaria", "Berlin"]`

Matching logic:
- Build `servedSet` from `Object.keys(servedRegions)`
- For each rendered country path:
  - `isServed = servedSet.has(country.code)`

Color rules:
- Served country fill: `var(--color-accent)`
- Non-served fill: `var(--color-export-country-muted)`
- Active/hover stroke becomes stronger and brighter


4. Interaction Model
--------------------
4.1 Desktop behavior
- Hover on served country:
  - sets `activeCountry`
  - computes tooltip coordinates relative to map container
  - shows `MapTooltip` with country name + regions list
- Mouse move updates tooltip position smoothly
- Mouse leave clears active state and hides tooltip

4.2 Mobile behavior
- Mobile detection via media query:
  - `(hover: none), (pointer: coarse)`
- Tap on served country opens `MobileRegionModal`
- Modal content:
  - country name
  - bullet list of served states/regions
- Overlay/close button dismisses modal

4.3 Keyboard accessibility
- Served countries are keyboard-focusable (`tabIndex=0`)
- Enter/Space triggers selection same as click
- Non-served countries are non-interactive (`tabIndex=-1`)


5. Tooltip and Modal Components
-------------------------------
Tooltip component:
- `src/components/home/export-regions/MapTooltip.jsx`
- Responsibility:
  - presentation-only floating card
  - receives `countryName`, `regions`, `position`
- Styling:
  - dark blue surface
  - white text
  - rounded corners
  - subtle shadow
  - fade animation

Mobile modal component:
- `src/components/home/export-regions/MobileRegionModal.jsx`
- Responsibility:
  - presentation-only bottom-sheet/modal for mobile tap flow
  - receives `isOpen`, `countryName`, `regions`, `onClose`


6. Home Section Integration
---------------------------
Homepage section file:
- `src/components/home/ExportExperience.jsx`

Integration details:
- Imports static served data from `src/constants/servedRegions.js`
- Renders section heading/subtitle and map card
- Uses:
  - `<ExportMap servedRegions={servedRegions} />`

Additional list/cards section:
- Uses `buildServedCountryList()` to render country-wise region chips
- Country name conversion handled by `getCountryNameFromCode()`


7. Theme Tokens and Styling
---------------------------
Theme token definitions in:
- `src/index.css`

Map-specific tokens:
- `--color-export-map-start`
- `--color-export-map-end`
- `--color-export-country-muted`
- `--color-export-tooltip-bg`

Usage:
- Container uses a dark blue gradient background (theme token based)
- Country colors and tooltip background use CSS variables (no hardcoded values in map logic)
- Transitions are applied via Tailwind utilities and inline style props where dynamic


